sp1-usb-audio

module/nrf-usbd-isofast/src/udc_nrf.c is Nordic Semiconductor ASA's nRF USBD
device-controller driver from Zephyr (drivers/usb/udc/udc_nrf.c), as carried by
nRF Connect SDK's Zephyr (sdk-zephyr, commit fd9204a0), Copyright (c) 2021
Nordic Semiconductor ASA, Apache-2.0. It has been MODIFIED: the changes are
exactly module/nrf-usbd-isofast/patches/udc_nrf-iso-in-fast.patch against the
unmodified copy in module/nrf-usbd-isofast/patches/udc_nrf.c.upstream.

sp1/fw/src/audio.c ports the SP-1 audio bring-up (TAS2505 and CS42L42
configuration, clock topology, init order, audio thread) from
chattock/sp1-tape-looper, firmware/src/main.c, at commit 2565e79,
Copyright (c) 2026 chattock, MIT License. The licence text is in
LICENSES/sp1-tape-looper-MIT.txt. The CS42L42 register sequence is Tim
Knapen's (github.com/timknapen/SP-1-dev/wiki/I2C).

sp1/prep.sh builds against two projects it fetches at build time and does not
include here: marisko's sp1 board definition (github.com/softmodded/marisko)
and feldd's hardware files (github.com/bnjreece/feldd-sp1-firmware, MIT,
Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Reece). Their licences govern those files.
